Navigate to Access Management by clicking on Access in the left sidebar.

Click on Roles to view the default system roles:

System Administrator: Full system access
System Auditor: Read-only access to all resources
Normal User: Basic user access
Review role permissions by clicking on each role to understand their capabilities.

Subtask 2.2: Create Custom User Roles
Create a new custom role by clicking the Add button in the Roles section.

Configure the "Project Manager" role:

Name: Project Manager
Description: Can manage projects and job templates
Assign specific permissions to the Project Manager role:

Permissions to assign:
- Project: Add, Change, Delete
- Job Template: Add, Change, Delete, Execute
- Inventory: View
- Credential: View (for assigned credentials only)
Create an "Operator" role:

Name: Operator
Description: Can execute jobs but not modify configurations
Permissions:
- Job Template: Execute, View
- Job: View
- Inventory: View
Save both custom roles by clicking Save for each.

